over the years you bazoft hasn't been  afraid to switch up the formula of its  uber popular action-adventure historical  park or further collecting franchise  assassin's creed there was the year they  dabbled some would say unsuccessfully  with tower defense that weird  hide-and-seek bit in assassin's creed 3  and of course who could forget newborn  simulator 2009 edition but now we're in  2014 an assassin's creed has made the  leap of faith to next generation  consoles with its latest edition unity  and with the jump comes a bunch of new  additions and changes to the norm so  here's 10 things to look out for on your  next outing in the Animus well let's  start with the most obvious addition  we've got a brand new assassin to take  for a tumble  Altea young Ezio slightly older Ezio old  Ezio Haytham Connor Aveline a Diwali and  Edward will miss you  young Connor will miss you most of all  but now it's Arno Dorian's time to shine  the French Austrian assassin comes  suited and booted with a gritty  backstory after his assassin father and  his Templar adopted father are murdered  with Arno framed for the latter crime he  embroiled himself in the French  Revolution to squeeze out or kill let's  just say kill the real troublemakers  he's brash charismatic and clearly has a  devastating case of the hansoms  which hasn't gone unnoticed he's having  an ill-fated love affair with his  adopted sister the Templar Elise de la  Sayer  every assassin comes with their own  unique addition to the regular Arsenal  our nose is the Phantom blade a wrists  bound mini crossbow that fires both  lethal and non-lethal projectiles but  can be used as a hidden blade in close  encounters so basically it's the Swiss  Army knife of wrist blades Abstergo are  dropping us off in Paris and it's  definitely worth taking the time to  admire the view rome wasn't built in a  day and neither was the French capital  UB spent 1287 days recreating the city  spending upwards of a year on the huge  landmark notre dam which was recreated  to an impressive one-to-one scale the  whole city is divided into distinct  districts each with their own aesthetic  and NPCs to boot in a Paris is roughly  to a one-to-one scale with the outer  limits of the city hitting around one to  six previous assassin games have been  very much outdoorsy affairs in ACU the  interiors of more than 25% of Paris's  buildings are explorable and you're able  to access them without hitting a single  load screen so if you add together the  map size plus the interiors and the  catacombs beneath the city you're  looking at a game that's three times  larger than Black Flag's landmass  hold down that right trigger because it  is freerunning time the new parkour up  and parkour down systems give you much  more control so you can pick the exact  path you want Arno to take along the  rooftops of Paris the new controlled  descent allows you to well control your  descent meaning you don't have to keep  an eye out for a haystack in order to  get back to street level as assassins  should neither be seen nor heard UB has  beefed up the usual stealth mechanics  for unity now at the touch of a button  Arno ducks into stealth mode where the  silent footballs make sneaking up on  enemies much easier not only that but  there's finally a decent cover system so  you can hug corners and duck behind  tables to your heart's content with a  splint to sell esque shadow of your last  known location left behind and if you  get busted the push to next-gen means  that the game can handle up to five  thousand NPCs on screen at one time so  mixing with a huge crowd to lose some  heat is a viable option  combats had a bit of a switch up most  notably kill streaks and counter kills  argon swordplay and ACU takes its  inspiration from fencing and is based  more on timing and flow you've still got  combat moves like the parry dodge tackle  and the returning heavy attack but you  need to keep your wits about you as the  AI has been beefed up too they can  overpower you quite quickly if you get  too cocky  and of course there's a ton of sidequest  content to fill your assassin boots with  Arno can solve various murders around  the city because apparently you get your  detectives license with your Brotherhood  induction pack there's collectibles  contracts to pick up life stories of  famous persons like Madame Tussauds to  uncover and Nostradamus quests the great  prophet lived in Paris for a time and an  ACU has left some clues around the city  to take any who follow them on a great  treasure hunt to find some sweet sweet  gubbins  we've played dress-up in Assassin's  before but the system goes much deeper  in unity mixing and matching our nose  gear can give great gameplay benefits  like increasing the time you can stay  hidden in a crowd or the strength of  your Eagle sense using XP gained by  completing missions you can specialize  in health ranged attacks stealth and  melee skills and gear you've equipped in  single player carry over into the story  based co-op missions so you're always  playing as your are no you can  specialize in one of four unique co-op  skills plan with your friends  accordingly and you become a formidable  team to get started just head to the  place where all the best laid plans are  formed the pub and if your friends ghost  is in there you can quickly join them to  either assassinate a foe or sabotage and  execution if your friends aren't online  you can be matched with strangers online  or have a crack at the mission yourself  Acey use mission structure is much more  fluid than previous installments there's  two main kinds the first of which the  adaptive mission mechanic or AMM adapts  to how you play so if you tale a guard  and get spotted the game automatically  switches from a tail mission into a  chase if you lose him it becomes a  locate mission which means there's no  more unfair D synchronizations the  second main mission type is the black  box a change to the regular  assassination the foe is plunked inside  a slice of the open world and then  you're let loose to create opportunities  and find your own path to the target the  mission doesn't end with a gurgling  speech in the killing blow you got  yourself in you have to be able to get  yourself out to  so there we have it 10 big new auditions  and switch ups to Assassin's Creed unity  which are you most excited about any big  changes you'd like to see where and when  would you like the series to go next let  me know in the comments for all the  latest historical assassinations make  sure you keep your eye on gamespot
 

